rc="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/konungs-skuggsja.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Konungs skuggsjá</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">Konungs skuggsjá (The King's Mirror) is an Old Norse educational work written in Norway around 1250, probably for the sons of King Haakon IV.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/konya"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/konya.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Konya</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Konya is a city in central Anatolia, the ancient Iconium.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/koos-de-la-rey"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/koos-de-la-rey.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Koos de la Rey</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Koos de la Rey was a Boer general of the South African Republic and one of the most successful commanders of the Second Boer War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kopek"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kopek.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Kopek</span><span class="enc-type">Term</span><span class="enc-snip">The kopek is a small unit of Russian currency, one hundredth of a rouble.</span></a></li></ul>
